                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "75698abc-655b-3d53-9a10-12fedfe73a65",
                        "entry_id": "0a668cfa-3567-3800-a5fc-51d58f09a84a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The bearing of an aircraft, usually relative to magnetic north, determined by omnidirectional radio signals."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e4c2b351-5816-4183-b50c-7d1fee0ec83e",
                                "sense_id": "75698abc-655b-3d53-9a10-12fedfe73a65",
                                "text": "Consequently the capsule could be positioned only by omnibearings reported from the capsule."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ab601bf-6202-4d86-9121-c34d62301cb4",
                                "sense_id": "75698abc-655b-3d53-9a10-12fedfe73a65",
                                "text": "By map reference and omnibearings, he erroneously estimated his position at E', and would have attempted to fly a heading away from the station had he not been corrected."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "04570e27-1248-4b52-90a8-77894cd8f190",
                                "sense_id": "75698abc-655b-3d53-9a10-12fedfe73a65",
                                "text": "Then a continuous readout of the omnibearing appears in the space used for frequency display, followed by an \"F\" when \"from\" is selected, for positive identification."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc7e7596-4ac6-42eb-bcc5-89ed5c0ca5a3",
                                "sense_id": "75698abc-655b-3d53-9a10-12fedfe73a65",
                                "text": "The bearing of the aircraft is shown in degrees on the aircraft's omnibearing selector. Left-right displacement from the bearing line is shown on the course-line-deviation indicator. To denote direction of the omnibearing line with respect to the VOR, a \"to-from\" ambiguity indicator is used."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
